0..76 Comment "// Second-order signatures written as their descriptions render them. A sort"
77..155 Comment "// classified `Type+` is representable, and a port `t : pi+ (x : S) . T` binds"
156..225 Comment "// a variable of the representable sort `S` over `T` (Kaposi and Xie,"
226..286 Comment "// _Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_, FSCD 2024,"
287..359 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10, Definition 3 and the identity-return"
360..436 Comment "// example). Each block is a value of `Theory` that keeps both, so a program"
437..466 Comment "// reads them back by `case`."
